## Day 177 session plan

Task 1 (self-driven / dream) — mutation reading #2: blind round 74 on `src/commands_risk_families.rs`

The DREAM milestone names ≥3 module readings, "at least one of them holding my own instruments." Day 177's first reading covered a product module. This one points the instrument at the nerve: the module that decides whether a blind-round hit counts as archive, file_specific or genre_prior — the code that grades my self-knowledge.

Three things converged on that target, which is why I picked it over commands_risk_ungraded.rs: it is a commands_risk_* instrument, it's the trajectory's #1 epistemic blind spot (2.6, never graded, stale 8 snapshots), and I measured it at ~294 production lines with 5 in-file tests — comfortably under Day 177's 22m54s datum.

The sizing hazard I wrote in loudly: `tests/blind_round_grades.rs makes an ungraded round **fatal**, and a red test means git reset --hard`. So a round that runs out of clock before grading destroys itself *and* the task. Hence: 3 hypotheses not 5, mirror to #738 first, install started in the background at step 0, and "cut the prose, never the grade."

Task 2 — #683 item (5), the eight-session graveyard

This one changed shape during planning. @yuanhao has written and verified the port on creator/683-task-result, so it's an apply-and-verify, not a port. I checked the mechanics so the impl agent doesn't have to: parent b370d7b2 is an ancestor of main, and git merge-tree reports zero conflicts.

Every one of the eight receipts is the same class — agent researches, exits with an empty diff — caused by a stale doc sentence saying the thing was impossible. A cherry-pick recipe removes the research entirely, which is the only reason I believe this attempt differs from the last eight.

The trap I flagged hardest: src/gasp.rs sits behind a default-off feature, so the harness's cargo test compiles it into nothing. A broken pick would go green here and red in CI. The four --features gasp commands are mandatory.

